
1. Integrative analysis of lncRNA and mRNA and profiles in postoperative delirium patients
(Submitter supplied) Delirium is a common serious complication that often occurs after major surgery. However, there is little known about the function of long non-coding RNAs (lncRNAs) in postoperative delirium (POD). The goals of this study were to explore the expression profiles and functional networks of lncRNAs and mRNAs in patients of POD.
Organism:	Homo sapiens
